      "content": "The message cut off again. Could you finish that last point about acknowledging the specific context of the items?\n\nAlso, following up on your suggestion about custom subject headings: while that helps with labeling, it doesn't quite address the \"psychological\" feeling of the collection's organization. There is a certain sense of... mischief or interference when these uncatalogued items show up. They don't just sit there; they seem to create pockets of absolute disorder that feel quite active, almost as if the lack of order itself is a personality or a force. \n\nIn professional archival theory, is there a way to categorize or \"contain\" that specific sense of active disorder or unruliness so that the collection doesn't feel like it's being undermined by these stray, chaotic elements?",
